I come back to the customer service counter.
I give the new shirt to him.
"This fits me," I say.
He looks at my old bill.
The first shirt was small for me.
This new shirt is bigger than that.
He adds the details in the computer.
It is very easy to exchange this shirt.
He puts the new shirt in a bag and gives it to me.
"Thank you very much," I say to him.
I step out of the store.
It is midday now.
There is still heavy rain outside.
I put on my new yellow raincoat.
To ride a bicycle in the rain, a raincoat is better than an umbrella.
I will not have trouble during this monsoon anymore.
I feel very relieved.
